{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvagbYtHzumXSGG9NY9h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: don't make the non-buyer survey the basis for the decision. Reshape the next step to find out why people bought and refunded, and whether the offer is wanted at all.**\n\n**Why the survey is weak**\n- The gap is about 10x (0.3% against 3%). Halving the price would rarely lift take-up tenfold, so price probably isn't the main problem.\n- Stated willingness to pay is unreliable. Non-buyers say \"I'd pay less\" cheaply, and the people who answer a survey aren't representative.\n- The 40% refund rate is the more important signal. Net take-up is about 0.18%, and people who did buy mostly found it wasn't what they expected. That points to a value or expectation problem, not just price.\n\n**What I'd do instead (a few weeks, low cost)**\n1. **Check the funnel.** How many people actually saw the offer, clicked through and reached checkout? If few saw it, the 0.3% says more about placement than demand.\n2. **Talk to the buyers and refunders.** With 0.3% of 20,000 (at most about 60 buyers, fewer if only half were shown the offer), that's a small group you can interview directly. Ask what they expected, what they got and why they refunded.\n3. **Check the economics.** Compare the cost to serve with the net revenue per customer. This tells you what price would be viable before you test any.\n4. **Ask a small group of non-buyers a different question.** Ask about the problem (how they get support today, how much it bothers them) rather than \"would you pay less?\"\n\n**Decision rule:** if refunders cite a mismatch with expectations, fix the proposition first. If the funnel and interviews show real demand at a viable price, run a randomised price test with two or three price points. Otherwise, park the add-on."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3449,"cache_read_input_tokens":5010,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3449},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"259b308c-54a6-4eff-85ba-e059e1ae7ef7","uuid":"0c7a94c7-49d2-422c-80ff-43a6b2f647a3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:08:46.567Z","request_id":"req_011CfvagbJWbT8J8FJGK3bMZ"}
